    // Easier: let clap handle all parsing, and we only intercept help/version when they appear in valid positions. We can attempt to use clap's try_get_matches, and if it returns DisplayHelp or DisplayVersion, we print our custom help/version strings instead of clap's default.
    // Let's try that approach: call cmd.try_get_matches_from, match error kind.
    let args_for_clap: Vec<String> = args.clone();
